text:
ryan: dropped an SSG starter that demos embeddings + ISR + on-demand revalidate. hitting 401s only when Vercel calls the /api/revalidate route during ISR, and the SDK logs repeated retries. repo: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-ssg-embed-starter

olivia: can you paste the revalidate API and the environment usage?

ryan: simplified route:
```js
// pages/api/revalidate.js
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk'
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_REDWOOD_KEY })
export default async function handler(req,res){
  // on-demand revalidate triggered by Vercel
  await client.embeddings.create({ model: 'e2-mini', input: 'ping' })
  res.status(200).end('ok')
}
```
logs show: `Request to /api/revalidate failed: 401 Unauthorized` then `redwood-sdk-js retrying request (attempt 4)`

meera: two things: 1) NEXT_PUBLIC_* can be baked into SSG builds and sometimes ends up in server bundles for revalidate endpoints depending on build/runtime; never use PUBLIC keys for server SDK calls. 2) the SDK retry wrapper treats 401 like a transient error by default which makes the logs noisy and can overload the backend during bad key rotations.

olivia: short fixes: switch to a server-only env var and make the revalidate route bail on auth errors without retry. Example:
```js
// pages/api/revalidate.js
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk'
const client = new RedwoodClient({
  apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY,
  retry: { statusCodes: [429, 502, 503], maxRetries: 1 }
})
export default async function handler(req,res){
  try {
    await client.embeddings.create({ model: 'e2-mini', input: 'ping' })
    res.status(200).end('ok')
  } catch (err) {
    if (err.status === 401) return res.status(401).end('invalid key')
    throw err
  }
}
```

ryan: made the switch, redeployed, and the revalidate flow is green. Also added a tiny CI smoke test that calls the revalidate endpoint with a mocked client to catch PUBLIC key usage and an integration test that asserts the route returns 200 for a valid stubbed key. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-ssg-embed-starter/pull/17

devex-bot: Created issue #88 in next-ssg-embed-starter: "Avoid NEXT_PUBLIC_* for revalidate routes; don't retry on 401; add CI smoke for revalidate"

ryan: thanks for the quick help. will also add a short README note about how ISR/revalidate runs can surface build-time env pitfalls. closing loop.
